<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Dexia retail share placement closed early.</title>
<headline>Belgian Dexia retail share placement closed early.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Retail subscriptions to a follow-up issue of shares in Dexia Belgium, the Belgian arm of Belgian-French banking group Dexia, were closed ahead of schedule, the group said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Dexia Belgium, which controls Credit Communal de Belgique (CCB) and Credit Local de France (CLF), said demand well exceeded supply of 2.47 million shares.</p>
<p>The maximum price for the additional shares is 3,825 francs, which compares with Thursday's Brussels bourse close of 3,915. The final price will be announced on June 26, when the issue starts trading.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
